A||||3||GoCartGuy||3.4 Swap?||||1||
Z||000000||GoCartGuy||05-08-2001||01:42 AM||||Ok, before everyone jumps on me for this, I already used the search function and out of the 104 posts I could not find all the answers I wanted.<P>First the Stats.<BR>1985 GT 2.8 V-6, tranny is a 3 speed auto with the torque converter, (installed by previous owner), no A/C, Koni Coil Over adjustables in the back<P>Now the questions.<BR>1.) Can I swap out the 3.4l pushrod from a 93-95 Camaro/Firebird and keep my existing tranny?<BR>2.) Which heads to I use, the aluminum ones off the 3.4 or the iron ones off the 2.8?  No one seems to agree on this?<BR>3.) Which ECM the Fiero or the donor?<BR>4.) Can I use a custom made cold air intake similar to the one West Coast sells with the 3.4?<BR>5.) Besides the normal bolt ons from the 2.8, and the cutting of the block to fit the tranny what other mods am I looking at to do the swap?<P>Thanx in advance, lookin to do the swap this summer/fall.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000001||RedOktober||05-08-2001||01:58 AM||||To Answer some of your questions.. <BR>1) Yes...<BR>2) The iron ones from the stock 2.8 <BR>3) The stock ECM will do fine. <BR>4) What ever will fit on the 2.8 can be used with the 3.4 including Design1's Turbo Kit, Supercharger,  Cold air intakes, Etc.. You are basically using the 2.8 's upper, middle and lower intake. <BR>5) recommend talking to Ed Parks or visiting his web page. he has a great write up and give good details..<P>Happy hunting for a good donor engine....they are getting rare. None in my area for the last 3 months. <P><P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-08-2001||07:25 AM||||Take a look at these links.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||05-08-2001||04:48 PM||||You will need to drill the holes and mount the starter to the other side of the block. You will need a neutrally balanced flywheel or flex plate unless you have an 88 fiero. The 93-95 3.4-liter Camaro engine has iron heads. If you get a motor with aluminum heads than you cannot just bolt on your iron heads because the pistons are different. There is a pressure relief valve in the oil passage of you 2.8 that may not be in the 3.4. You need to transfer this valve if it’s not there. You will need to modify your front engine mount and get an adapter for the oil pressure sending gauge. <P>George Miller from the Fieroshop or Ed Parks can help you with the starter holes and the front motor mount.  <P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 05-08-2001).]||||reg||1
